            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous duodenal hematoma in a patient with Glanzmann's thrombasthenia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1341-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous intramural duodenal hematoma is a rare problem, most commonly seen in children who have coagulation disorders. A child who had Glanzmann's thrombasthenia, a disorder of platelet function, presented with signs and symptoms of duodenal obstruction. Nonoperative management of an obstructing duodenal hematoma was successful and potentially life-threatening surgery was avoided.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
